In /tmp/sv-aa803417d30c42d893c3c246ddc8738c/before, fix these special AOT compatibility issues:

## 1. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs
The method at line 27 calls `builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration)` which is marked with [RequiresUnreferencedCode] and [RequiresDynamicCode]. Add both attributes to the method.

Edit `/tmp/sv-aa803417d30c42d893c3c246ddc8738c/before/Extensions/ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs`:
Change:
```
        /// <summary>
        /// Registers an <see cref="ArmClient"/> instance with connection options loaded from the provided <paramref name="configuration"/> instance.
        /// </summary>
        public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
            where TBuilder : IAzureClientFactoryBuilderWithConfiguration<TConfiguration>
```
To:
```
        /// <summary>
        /// Registers an <see cref="ArmClient"/> instance with connection options loaded from the provided <paramref name="configuration"/> instance.
        /// </summary>
        [RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
        [RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime, for example instantiating generic types.")]
        public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
            where TBuilder : IAzureClientFactoryBuilderWithConfiguration<TConfiguration>
```

Also add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to the existing usings if not already there. Check first:
The file currently has:
```
using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;
```
at line 4, so it's already there. Good.

## 2. ArmOperation.cs - Fix IL2087/IL2090

The `IsResource<T>()` method uses reflection on `typeof(T)`. Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` to the generic type parameter.

The method signature at line 96 is:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<T>() where T : notnull
```

Change it to:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

Also, the callers `Rehydrate<T>` (line 44) and `RehydrateAsync<T>` (line 82) need the same annotation on their `T` parameter since they pass T to IsResource<T> and new GenericOperationSource<T>.

Change line 44:
```csharp
        public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull
```
To:
```csharp
        public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull
```

Change line 82:
```csharp
        public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull
```
To:
```csharp
        public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull
```

Also add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` at the top of ArmOperation.cs. The file currently has these usings:
```
using System.ClientModel.Primitives;
using System.Reflection;
using System;
using Azure.Core;
using Azure.Core.Pipeline;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
```
Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` after `using System.Reflection;`.

## 3. GenericOperationSource.cs - Fix IL2087

The class `GenericOperationSource<T>` uses `typeof(T)` with reflection. Add annotation to the type parameter.

Change line 16:
```csharp
    internal class GenericOperationSource<T> : IOperationSource<T>
```
To:
```csharp
    internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

The file already has `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` at line 8.

## 4. ArmEnvironment.cs - Fix JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)

Line 80: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

ArmEnvironment is a simple struct with `Uri Endpoint` and `string Audience`. Replace with manual JSON:
```csharp
        public override string ToString()
        {
            return $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\"}}";
        }
```

## 5. ArmClientOptions.cs - Fix JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<...>>

Line 52: `var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);`

Replace with using JsonDocument to parse and manually build the dictionary:
```csharp
                var jsonDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
                var allProfile = new Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>();
                foreach (var prop in jsonDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
                {
                    var inner = new Dictionary<string, JsonElement>();
                    foreach (var innerProp in prop.Value.EnumerateObject())
                    {
                        inner[innerProp.Name] = innerProp.Value.Clone();
                    }
                    allProfile[prop.Name] = inner;
                }
```

Look at the full context of ArmClientOptions.cs around line 52 to understand what to replace. The current code is:
```csharp
                var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;
                var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
```

Replace those two lines with:
```csharp
                var jsonDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
                var allProfile = new Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>();
                foreach (var prop in jsonDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
                {
                    var inner = new Dictionary<string, JsonElement>();
                    foreach (var innerProp in prop.Value.EnumerateObject())
                    {
                        inner[innerProp.Name] = innerProp.Value.Clone();
                    }
                    allProfile[prop.Name] = inner;
                }
```

Make sure to add `using System.Collections.Generic;` if not already present in ArmClientOptions.cs. Check first.

